Function \f(CW\*(C`fish/fish.c:win_prefix\*(C'\fR
.IX Subsection "Function fish/fish.c:win_prefix"
.PP
.Vb 2
\& char *
\& win_prefix (const char *path)
.Ve
.PP
Resolve the special \f(CW\*(C`win:...\*(C'\fR form for Windows\-specific paths.
The generated code calls this for all device or path arguments.
.PP
The function returns a newly allocated string, and the caller must
free this string; else display an error and return \f(CW\*(C`NULL\*(C'\fR.
.PP
Function \f(CW\*(C`fish/fish.c:file_in\*(C'\fR
.IX Subsection "Function fish/fish.c:file_in"
.PP
.Vb 2
\& char *
\& file_in (const char *arg)
.Ve
.PP
Resolve the special \f(CW\*(C`FileIn\*(C'\fR paths (\f(CW\*(C`\-\*(C'\fR or \f(CW\*(C`\-<<END\*(C'\fR or filename).
.PP
The caller (\fIfish/cmds.c\fR) will call \f(CW\*(C`free_file_in\*(C'\fR after the
command has run which should clean up resources.
.PP
Function \f(CW\*(C`fish/fish.c:file_out\*(C'\fR
.IX Subsection "Function fish/fish.c:file_out"
.PP
.Vb 2
\& char *
\& file_out (const char *arg)
.Ve
.PP
Resolve the special \f(CW\*(C`FileOut\*(C'\fR paths (\f(CW\*(C`\-\*(C'\fR or filename).
.PP
The caller (\fIfish/cmds.c\fR) will call \f(CW\*(C`free\ (str)\*(C'\fR after the
command has run.
.PP
Function \f(CW\*(C`fish/fish.c:progress_callback\*(C'\fR
.IX Subsection "Function fish/fish.c:progress_callback"
.PP
.Vb 5
\& void
\& progress_callback (guestfs_h *g, void *data,
\&                    uint64_t event, int event_handle, int flags,
\&                    const char *buf, size_t buf_len,
\&                    const uint64_t *array, size_t array_len)
