\fIFile fish/glob.c\fR
.IX Subsection "File fish/glob.c"
.PP
This file implements the guestfish \f(CW\*(C`glob\*(C'\fR command.
.PP
Function \f(CW\*(C`fish/glob.c:expand_devicename\*(C'\fR
.IX Subsection "Function fish/glob.c:expand_devicename"
.PP
.Vb 2
\& static char **
\& expand_devicename (guestfs_h *g, const char *device)
.Ve
.PP
Glob\-expand device patterns, such as \f(CW\*(C`/dev/sd*\*(C'\fR
(https://bugzilla.redhat.com/635971).
.PP
There is no \f(CW\*(C`guestfs_glob_expand_device\*(C'\fR function because the
equivalent can be implemented using functions like
\&\f(CW\*(C`guestfs_list_devices\*(C'\fR.
.PP
It\*(Aqs not immediately clear what it means to expand a pattern like
\&\f(CW\*(C`/dev/sd*\*(C'\fR.  Should that include device name translation?  Should
the result include partitions as well as devices?
.PP
Should \f(CW"/dev/"\fR + \f(CW"*"\fR return every possible device and
filesystem?  How about VGs?  LVs?
.PP
To solve this what we do is build up a list of every device,
partition, etc., then glob against that list.
.PP
Notes for future work (XXX):
.IP \(bu 4
This doesn\*(Aqt handle device name translation.  It wouldn\*(Aqt be
too hard to add.
.IP \(bu 4
Could have an API function for returning all device\-like things.
.PP
Function \f(CW\*(C`fish/glob.c:add_strings_matching\*(C'\fR
.IX Subsection "Function fish/glob.c:add_strings_matching"
.PP
.Vb 3
\& static int
\& add_strings_matching (char **pp, const char *glob,
\&                       char ***ret, size_t *size_r)
.Ve
.PP
Using POSIX \fBfnmatch\fR\|(3), find strings in the list \f(CW\*(C`pp\*(C'\fR which
match pattern \f(CW\*(C`glob\*(C'\fR.  Add strings which match to the \f(CW\*(C`ret\*(C'\fR
array.  \f(CW*size_r\fR is the current size of the \f(CW\*(C`ret\*(C'\fR array, which
is updated with the new size.
.PP
Function \f(CW\*(C`fish/glob.c:single_element_list\*(C'\fR
.IX Subsection "Function fish/glob.c:single_element_list"
.PP
.Vb 2
\& static char **
\& single_element_list (const char *element)
.Ve
.PP
Return a single element list containing \f(CW\*(C`element\*(C'\fR.
.PP
